This project follows the dual-license model used by the upstream
Formula Student Korea Electric Energy Meter project.

1. For non-commercial use:

   -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
   "THE BEER-WARE LICENSE" (Revision 42):
   luftaquila wrote the original Formula Student Korea Electric Energy Meter
   project. As long as you retain this notice, you can do whatever you want with
   the non-commercially licensed portions of this stuff. If you meet the original
   author someday, and you think this stuff is worth it, you can buy them a beer
   in return.
   -----------------------------------------------------------------------------

   FT26 EnergyMeter Logger modifications and project-specific additions are
   distributed under the same non-commercial Beer-Ware style terms unless a
   separate written license states otherwise.

2. For commercial use:

   Commercial use requires a separate commercial license from the applicable
   rights holders.

   The original Formula Student Korea Electric Energy Meter project states:

     You must obtain a separate commercial license from the author.
     Please contact mail@luftaquila.io for commercial licensing options.

   For FT26-specific modifications, firmware, viewer changes, documentation, and
   project-specific integration work, obtain separate written permission from the
   FT26 EnergyMeter Logger rights holder as well.

Third-party dependencies retain their own licenses. See package manifests,
dependency lockfiles, and NOTICE.md where applicable.
